Tool: VS Code Remote SSH
Purpose: Edit server files directly from your laptop
Installation: code --install-extension ms-vscode-remote.remote-ssh  (type command on terminal)

--setup---
--Connect VS Code to our Ubuntu server--

We'll use the Remote SSH extension to connect to the vm as vmuser.
Open the SSH connection menu
	1. Open VS Code.
	2. Press Ctrl + Shift + P to open the Command Palette.
	3. Type "Remote-SSH: Connect to Host..." and select it.
	4. Choose "Add New SSH Host..." if the server name isn't already listed.
When prompted for the SSH connection command, enter:  "ssh server-username@server-ip"
VS Code will ask where to save the SSH configuration. Select: "/<home>/directory/.ssh/config" 
